<title>INDIA: INDIAN SOYBEANS EASE SLIGHTLY, PROCESSORS BACK OFF.</title>
<headline>INDIAN SOYBEANS EASE SLIGHTLY, PROCESSORS BACK OFF.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were slightly down on limited purchasing from processing plants against good supply. Prices were down by 100 rupees per tonne today. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on good demand in the local market. Soyoil solvent was up 200 rupees and soyoil refined was up 100 rupees per tonne today. Business volume was dull, but the undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in thin trading as export demand was poor. Soymeal yellow was $264-265 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $95-96 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
